      "provenance": {
        "notes": "NAME CLASH: sentry palm Howea belmoreana is slower and recurved, and nurseries sell several seedlings per pot even though the plant is single-stemmed. Not a sago palm (deadly to pets). Watering: NC State wants a well-drained, humus-rich mix that does not dry out; RHS says moderate in growth and sparing in winter; mapped to keep_moist (agent), the page gives no schedule. Light: NC State says it survives low light and wants moderate light, avoid direct sun; RHS says bright light protected from sun (partial shade, north or east aspect); stored bright_indirect from RHS. Temperature: RHS hardiness H1A means under glass all year, above 15 C; the minimum 15 is the agent's reading of that scale. Humidity: RHS moderate, no figure. Size left unknown: RHS gives 2 m in the description but 8 to 12 m (spread 4 to 8 m) in the table and no spread for the indoor figure; NC State gives only frond length. Habit: NC State erect single stem; RHS lists 'bushy'. Toxicity: ASPCA lists it as non-toxic to dogs and cats and NC State tags it the same."
      },
